From: conda-forge hkl-feedstock maintainers
Date: 2026-05-26
Subject: [ccan/coroutine] Bump COROUTINE_MIN_STKSZ to satisfy macOS 11+ MINSIGSTKSZ

`hkl/ccan/coroutine/coroutine.c` contains a BUILD_ASSERT that
COROUTINE_MIN_STKSZ (defined in coroutine.h as 2048) is at least as
large as the platform's MINSIGSTKSZ:

    coroutine.c:63:    BUILD_ASSERT(COROUTINE_MIN_STKSZ >= MINSIGSTKSZ);

On macOS 11 SDK, <sys/signal.h> defines MINSIGSTKSZ=32768 (32 KiB),
while COROUTINE_MIN_STKSZ remains 2048, so the build assert fails:

    coroutine/coroutine.c:63:2: error: array size is negative
       63 |    BUILD_ASSERT(COROUTINE_MIN_STKSZ >= MINSIGSTKSZ);

The doc comment for COROUTINE_MIN_STKSZ explicitly promises:
"On systems with MINSTKSZ, guaranteed to be at least as large as
MINSTKSZ." -- i.e. the literal `2048` is a bug, not a deliberate
contract. Larger stacks are always safe; this only consumes slightly
more memory per coroutine instance.

Fix: bump the literal to 32768. This matches the actual macOS 11
MINSIGSTKSZ and is still well below typical stack-size guidance for
process threads, so impact is negligible.

A more general upstream fix would compute the value via #if defined
gates against the headers, but this is sufficient for the conda-forge
target platforms.

--- a/hkl/ccan/coroutine/coroutine.h
+++ b/hkl/ccan/coroutine/coroutine.h
@@ -50,7 +50,11 @@
  * overhead).  On systems with MINSTKSZ, guaranteed to be at least as
  * large as MINSTKSZ.
  */
-#define COROUTINE_MIN_STKSZ		2048
+/* Bumped from 2048 to 32768 to satisfy macOS 11+ MINSIGSTKSZ
+ * (sys/signal.h on macOS 11 SDK defines MINSIGSTKSZ=32768).
+ * BUILD_ASSERT in coroutine.c checks COROUTINE_MIN_STKSZ >= MINSIGSTKSZ.
+ * Larger stack size is always safe; only uses slightly more memory per coroutine. */
+#define COROUTINE_MIN_STKSZ		32768
 
